            <div xml:id="d806">

                <pb facs="0749" n="737" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg737"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111 A.R./1088: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-17T17:00:00-03:30">May 17, 1940—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>73. My 72, May 17, noon. Instead of the message mentioned in my telegram under
                    reference Guani is now cabling Panama that he <pb facs="0750" n="738"
                        xml:id="pg738"/> has just heard that Argentina has definitively withdrawn
                    its proposed modification and that Chile will reply tonight. He is requesting
                    the Panamanian Government to advise him of the nature of the Chilean reply and
                    whether Nicaragua has as yet replied. After hearing from Panama he will then
                    urge that the protest be published tomorrow with the names of the countries
                    accepting it and such observations as any of them may have made. He would
                    appreciate it if you would request our Legation at Managua to urge the
                    Nicaraguan Government to reply favorably to Panama tonight.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
